# Volcano Island Terrain Mesh
# A terrain with varied slope angles for testing
# Includes: flat areas, gentle slopes, moderate slopes, steep areas, cliffs

# Flat plateau vertices (y=0 plane)
v 0.0 0.0 0.0
v 4.0 0.0 0.0
v 4.0 0.0 4.0
v 0.0 0.0 4.0

# Gentle slope vertices (~18 degrees, rise=1.3 over run=4)
v 8.0 1.3 0.0
v 8.0 1.3 4.0

# Moderate slope vertices (~35 degrees, rise=2.8 over run=4)
v 12.0 4.1 0.0
v 12.0 4.1 4.0

# Steep slope vertices (~60 degrees, rise=6.93 over run=4)
v 16.0 11.03 0.0
v 16.0 11.03 4.0

# Near-vertical cliff vertices (~82 degrees, rise=28.6 over run=4)
v 20.0 39.63 0.0
v 20.0 39.63 4.0

# Additional flat area at height (for path testing)
v 20.5 40.0 8.0
v 16.0 11.03 8.0
v 12.0 4.1 8.0
v 8.0 1.3 8.0
v 0.0 0.0 8.0
v 4.0 0.0 8.0

# Flat plateau faces (CCW winding for upward normals)
f 1 3 2
f 1 4 3

# Gentle slope faces
f 2 6 5
f 2 3 6

# Moderate slope faces
f 5 8 7
f 5 6 8

# Steep slope faces
f 7 10 9
f 7 8 10

# Near-vertical cliff faces
f 9 12 11
f 9 10 12

# Back-side faces (connecting to additional vertices)
f 12 13 11
f 10 14 12
f 8 15 10
f 6 16 8
f 3 17 6
f 4 18 3

# Top connecting faces
f 12 14 13
f 10 15 14
f 8 16 15
f 6 17 16
f 3 17 18
